## Package Management

This project uses `bun` as both runtime and package manager (not npm or yarn).

```bash
bun install                  # Install all dependencies
bun add <package>            # Add a new dependency
bun add -d <package>         # Add a dev dependency
```

## Make Commands

### Development
```bash
make all              # Install deps and run main application
make dev              # Run in watch mode
make docs             # Run docs site locally
make onboard          # Interactive onboarding CLI
```

### Testing
```bash
make test             # Run all tests (bun test)
make test_fast        # Run fast tests (5s timeout)
make test_watch       # Run tests in watch mode
```

### Code Quality
```bash
make fmt              # Format code with Biome (auto-fix)
make lint             # Run Biome linter (check only)
make deadcode         # Find dead code + unused deps with knip
make typecheck        # TypeScript type checker (tsc --noEmit)
make tech_debt        # Check TODO/FIXME markers
make duplicate_code   # Detect duplicate code blocks
make import_lint      # Enforce module boundaries (dependency-cruiser)
make lint_links       # Check markdown links
make ci               # Run ALL CI checks (must pass before committing)
```

## Directory Structure

- `src/` - Source code (entrypoint: `src/index.ts`)
  - `src/config/` - Configuration loading, schemas, flags, LLM API key utils
  - `src/utils/` - Shared utilities (e.g., redact)
- `tests/` - Test files (bun:test), mirrors src/ structure
- `docs/` - Documentation site (Next.js/Fumadocs, separate dependency tree)
- `frontend/` - Frontend app (Vite/React, separate dependency tree)
- `scripts/` - Build/generation scripts (banner, logo, validation)

## Configuration

- Runtime config via `process.env` for secrets
- Structured config via Zod schemas in `src/config/schemas.ts`
- Config loading in `src/config/loader.ts`
- Feature flags in `src/config/flags.ts`

## CI Gate

**Always run `make ci` before committing.** It must pass with zero errors. If `make ci` is too slow for iterative work, run at minimum:

1. `make fmt` (auto-fix formatting)
2. `make lint` (check for errors)
3. `make typecheck` (verify types)

## Git Workflow

- `main` is protected — use PRs, never push directly
- Squash and merge strategy
- Never force push
- See `commit_msg.mdc` for commit message conventions
